165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Across 25 years of data, human error, directly or indirectly, accounted for a staggering 67% to 80% of all downtime incidents. The most common cause of major human error-related outages is data center staff failing to follow established procedures or processes, responsible for 48% of such incidents. This is followed by incorrect processes being implemented by staff \(45%\) and installation issues \(23%\). The repercussions of these errors are exemplified by significant financial losses reported in 2021 due to outages. Amazon lost an estimated $34 million in revenue during a one-hour outage, Facebook lost $100 million due to a five-hour disruption, and Alibaba faced a staggering $1 billion loss from a 20-minute outage on their most important day of the year: Singles Day.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
